<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Argonauta argo Schnakenberg critical mode at the 95 µm Holocene tier — Code-to-model traceability: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "jacobian, sigma_max, critical_wavenumber, mode_intensity, and measure_morphoeval are the docstring equations in code order. The math-KG file names the Lean theorems. Grain is isolated in procedural_grain and is not folded into k_c. Still no numbered equation tags from the 1952 paper." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Argonauta argo Schnakenberg critical mode at the 95 µm Holocene tier — Model fidelity to source: 87/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Same linearisation as pass 1: trace=-0.2, det=1, k_c=0.610, σ(k_c)=0.200, equal-diffusion σ_max=-0.100, eigenvalue cross-check r=1, five Lean theorems with zero sorry. Pass 2 does not change the PDE. The grain term is declared as sub-wavelength texture, outside k_c. Remaining deduction: diffusivities are calibrated to the plate period, and the spatial shape is the fitted critical mode rather than an untuned 2D time-stepper." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-argonauta-argo-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Argonauta argo Schnakenberg critical mode at the 95 µm Holocene tier — Morphometric validation: 87/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Plate versus mode: Pearson r 0.99934 (gate 0.98), RMSE 0.00550, residual CV 0.0118, KS D 0.063. Halo 85.87 µm versus tier reference 95 µm (not set equal); the 150 px window gives 85.29 µm. Plate coherency 0.203 versus grained-model coherency 0.290 (smooth-model coherency 0.998 is retained only as the pass-1 gap). Shell rib fraction 0.088 versus ocellus period fraction 0.234. Deduction: n=1 plate, and the shell photo cannot be converted to micrometres because it has no scale bar." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
